CORRECTIONS AFTER THE FIRST BUILD
(read this first)
MOCKUPS ARE THE LAW. Build exactly what the mockup pictures and the numbers in this document
show: the same spacing, sizes, icons, colours, corners, order of items and texts. Do not invent
anything that is not described here. Do not add, remove, move, resize, recolour or rename anything
because it seems better. Do not use a library default look (Material default colours, shapes, icon sets,
fonts, elevations) where this document gives a value. If something is missing or two things seem to
disagree, keep the existing behaviour of the app, copy the closest mockup, and ask. Before you call a
screen finished, put your screenshot next to the mockup picture and compare spacing, icons and text
one by one. Everything in the pictures that is a name, number or list is an example and must come
from real data.

These points come from the first screenshots of the build. They override anything shorter or different
further down.

1. Colour. The accent is blurple #5865F2. The build uses bright blue on the selected rail tile, Sign in
button, links and tab chip. Use only CcTheme.colors.accent. Search the code for any hard-coded
blue and remove it.

2. Panel action buttons. In the panel title area, New file and New folder (and any refresh or other
action) are each a 38 by 38 rounded button, radius 12, grey field colour #E9EBEF, with the icon
18 inside. Bare icons are wrong. Same for the header actions on full screens.

3. Swipe. The sidebar opens with a right swipe from anywhere on the editor, not only the edge. It
works when the swipe is mostly horizontal and the code cannot scroll further left. The left 40
dp edge always works. See Part 1, section 3, and SidebarHost in Part 2.

4. File tree. Names must always be visible. Indent is 10 dp per level (not 16), no vertical guide
lines, folders with a single folder inside are joined (src/main, java/com/app), and the name gets all
the remaining width with an ellipsis.

5. Buttons and text. Buttons never wrap and never cut their label with "...". Use short labels ("Sign
in", "Clone from link"). Empty-state sentences may wrap, buttons may not.

6. Run card. The panel is 234 dp wide. The Run button is a 40 by 40 green icon-only button (play
icon). The project name column takes the rest and is cut with an ellipsis. Nothing overlaps. See
Run card in Components and RunCard in Part 2.

7. Dim layer and sidebar width. Behind the sliding editor card use 30% of #1E2332, not a dark grey.
The card must still look light. The sidebar is 300 dp wide (rail 66 + panel 234), so the editor
card slides 300 dp to the right and only a 60 dp strip of it stays visible. In the first build the
card stopped at 250 dp, which left the panel too narrow (buttons cut off, names squeezed). The
middle layer (the panel) must be a rounded card: both its top-left and its top-right corners are
rounded, radius 26, exactly as in the mockups. In the first build the top-right corner of the
panel was square. That is wrong. The editor card keeps its rounded left corners. The panel's
own top-left corner is also rounded, radius 26, exactly as in the mockups.

8. Existing chips (for example the OPEN list). Keep them, but they scroll sideways and cut long
names with an ellipsis, never show half a word.

9. Tool highlight. In the rail, the highlighted tool must always match the panel that is showing. If a
tool opens a full screen instead of a panel, do not move the highlight.



