3. The swipe (exact behaviour)

The user can start the swipe anywhere on the editor, not only at the edge. A drag counts as
"open the sidebar" when it moves to the right, is mostly horizontal (sideways movement more than
twice the up or down movement, after a 10 dp touch slop), AND the editor content under the finger
cannot scroll further left (the code is not scrolled sideways, or the finger is on the tab row, the
header or an empty area).
If the code view IS scrolled sideways, a right swipe first scrolls the code back. A swipe that starts
in the left 40 dp edge always opens the sidebar, even then.
Vertical drags and upward or downward scrolling are never taken by the sidebar.
A drag to the left while the sidebar is closed does nothing here (the editor keeps it).
The editor card follows the finger. Progress goes 0.0 to 1.0 over 300 dp.
While dragging: translationX = 300 dp * progress, the card's left corners get radius 26 dp * progress,
scrim (dark layer) 0.30 * progress.
On release: open if progress > 0.4 or the fling velocity to the right is above 800 dp/s. Close if
progress < 0.4 or the fling goes left.
Settle with spring(dampingRatio = 0.85f, stiffness = 400f).
While open, the card ignores taps on its content. A tap anywhere on the card closes the sidebar.
The sidebar is NOT opened by a button. No hamburger icon.
When the keyboard is up, the swipe is disabled.

