Always check LocalReduceMotion / Settings.Global.ANIMATOR_DURATION_SCALE. If the scale is 0, use snap()
instead of springs.



6. Data rules (real data, repeated because it matters)

Every list is a StateFlow or Flow from the real database or the real file system. Screens only display.
They never contain sample items.
A project's colour and letter: stored in the project table (colorHex, derived from the name if not set).
Letter is name.first().uppercase().
Times are formatted from real timestamps by one function relativeTime(millis).
If a list is empty, call EmptyState(...) (Part 2). If data is loading, call LoadingList(). If it failed, call ErrorC
ard(message, onRetry).

7. What your developer should NOT do

Do not add a menu button to open the sidebar.
Do not show the rail on full screens.
Do not keep a permanent text-labelled rail.
Do not invent projects, files, commits or users.
Do not change any logic. Only change how things look and how screens connect.

PART 2. THE CODE (Kotlin, Jetpack
Compose)
Package names and file names are suggestions. Put each block in its own file. Every block compiles
against Compose BOM 2024.09 or newer with Material 3. Nothing here contains sample data. Every
screen takes its data as parameters from the real ViewModel.

2.1 How icons are built (the letters and numbers)

The letters and numbers your developer sees (for example M15 18l-6-6 6-6) are SVG path data. It is a
tiny drawing language. Letters are commands, numbers are coordinates on a 24 by 24 grid:

Letter Meaning Example

M x y Move the pen to the point (no line) M15 18

L x y Draw a line to the point L9 12

l dx dy Draw a line, relative to the current point l-6-6 means 6 left, 6 up

H x, h dx Horizontal line H21

V y, v dy Vertical line v4

A rx ry rot large sweep x y Arc (curve of a circle) a2 2 0 0 1 2 2

C, c Curve

Z Close the shape



So M15 18l-6-6 6-6 means: go to (15,18), draw to the left-up, then draw right-up. That is the back
chevron "<". The Kotlin code can read this text directly. You do not draw the icons by hand and you
do not need a drawable file for each icon. Keep the path text in one list and build the vectors from it.

All icons: viewport 24 by 24, stroke only, stroke width 1.8 (2.2 chevrons, 2.4 ticks), round cap, round
join, no fill (Play is filled).

File ui/icons/CcIcons.kt

