02 Start a project (full screen)



Why: create a project from a template the app really ships. Behaviour: pick a template card (selected
card gets a 2 dp accent outline), type a name (validated: not empty, not already used), choose the
location, press Create. A progress bar shows while files are written, then the editor opens. Data: vm.te
mplates, vm.storageRoot.

@Composable

fun StartProjectScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val templates by vm.templates.collectAsState()

    var selected by remember { mutableStateOf(templates.firstOrNull()?.id) }

    var name by remember { mutableStateOf("") }

    val error = vm.nameError(name)

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Start a project", onBack)

        LazyVerticalGrid(GridCells.Fixed(2), Modifier.weight(1f), contentPadding = PaddingValues(16.dp),

            horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(10.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(10.dp)) {

            items(templates, key = { it.id }) { t ->

                val sel = t.id == selected

                Column(Modifier.clip(CcShape.card).background(c.field)

                    .border(if (sel) 2.dp else 0.dp, if (sel) c.accent else Color.Transparent, CcShape.card)

                    .clickable { selected = t.id }.padding(14.dp)) {

                    Box(Modifier.size(42.dp).clip(CcShape.tile).background(t.tint.tint()), contentAlignment = Alignment.Cen

ter) { CcIcon(t.icon, t.tint, 21.dp) }

                    Spacer(Modifier.height(10.dp))

                    OneLine(t.name, CcType.itemTitle, c.text)

                    OneLine(t.description, CcType.caption, c.muted)

                }

            }

        }

        Column(Modifier.padding(16.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(12.dp)) {

            CcTextField(name, { name = it }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), label = "Project name", hint = "my-app", error = if 

(name.isNotEmpty()) error else null)

            PrimaryButton("Create", { vm.create(selected!!, name) }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), enabled = selected != null && 

name.isNotBlank() && error == null)

        }

    }

}

03 Switch project (bottom sheet, layer 4)

Why: change the open project quickly. Behaviour: opens when the avatar at the top of the rail is
tapped. Lists the real projects, current one has a check. Buttons below start, clone or open. No
projects: the empty state. Data: vm.projects.

@Composable

fun ProjectSwitcherSheet(vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav) {

    val projects by vm.projects.collectAsState(); val current by vm.project.collectAsState()

    CcBottomSheet("Projects", onDismiss = { nav.sheet = null }) {

        if (projects.isEmpty()) EmptyState("folder", "No projects yet", "Start a project, clone one or open a folder.")

        else projects.forEach { p ->

            PanelRow("folder", p.color, p.name, relativeTime(p.lastOpened), selected = p.id == current?.id,

                onClick = { vm.open(p); nav.sheet = null; nav.closeSidebar() },

                trailing = if (p.id == current?.id) ({ CcIcon("check", CcTheme.colors.accent, 18.dp, 2.4f) }) else null)

        }

        Spacer(Modifier.height(12.dp))

        PrimaryButton("New project", { nav.sheet = null; nav.push(Route.StartProject) }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), icon = "p

lus")

        Spacer(Modifier.height(8.dp))

        Row(horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp)) {

            SecondaryButton("Open folder", { nav.sheet = null; vm.pickFolder() }, Modifier.weight(1f), icon = "folder")

            SecondaryButton("Clone", { nav.sheet = null; nav.push(Route.Clone) }, Modifier.weight(1f), icon = "branch")

        }

    }

}

04 Clone a repository, 05 Cloning progress (full screens)

Why: get a project from git. Behaviour: URL (mono) and optional branch. Clone starts a real git clone
and goes to the progress screen. Progress shows the real step text (Counting, Receiving, Resolving)



and percent. Cancel stops the process and deletes the half-cloned folder. On success the project
opens in the editor and the stack is cleared. On error the real message shows in an ErrorCard with
Retry. Data: vm.cloneState.

@Composable

fun CloneScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit, onStarted: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    var url by remember { mutableStateOf("") }; var branch by remember { mutableStateOf("") }

    val signedIn by vm.github.signedIn.collectAsState()

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Clone a repository", onBack)

        Column(Modifier.padding(16.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(14.dp)) {

            CcTextField(url, { url = it }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), label = "Repository link", hint = "https://github.com/u

ser/repo.git", mono = true, leadingIcon = "globe")

            CcTextField(branch, { branch = it }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), label = "Branch (optional)", hint = "main", mono 

= true, leadingIcon = "branch")

            if (!signedIn) Text("Private repositories need GitHub sign in.", style = CcType.caption, color = c.muted)

            PrimaryButton("Clone", { vm.startClone(url.trim(), branch.trim().ifEmpty { null }); onStarted() },

                Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), icon = "down", enabled = url.isNotBlank())

        }

    }

}

@Composable

fun CloningScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val s by vm.cloneState.collectAsState()

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(CcTheme.colors.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Cloning", onBack)

        Column(Modifier.padding(16.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(14.dp)) {

            when (val st = s) {

                is CloneState.Running -> { ProgressLine(st.step, st.percent / 100f, "${st.percent}%"); SecondaryButton("Can

cel", vm::cancelClone, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), destructive = true) }

                is CloneState.Failed -> ErrorCard(st.message, onRetry = vm::retryClone)

                else -> {}

            }

        }

    }

}

06 First-time setup (full screen)

Why: downloads build tools the app needs. Behaviour: each card is a tool the app really needs, with
real download progress, a tick when done and a Skip for optional ones. Finish is disabled (grey) until
the required cards are done. Data: vm.toolchain (list of tools with state Missing, Downloading(percent),
Ready).

@Composable

fun FirstSetupScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit, onFinish: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val tools by vm.toolchain.collectAsState()

    val canFinish = tools.filter { it.required }.all { it.state is ToolState.Ready }

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Set up", onBack)

        Column(Modifier.weight(1f).verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()).padding(horizontal = 22.dp, vertical = 20.dp)) {

            Text("CLOSECODE", style = CcType.section.copy(fontSize = 13.sp), color = c.accent)

            Text("Set up your build environment", style = CcType.setupTitle, color = c.text, modifier = Modifier.padding(to

p = 10.dp))

            Text("One-time downloads. You can skip any and add it later in Settings.", style = CcType.small.copy(fontSize = 

13.5.sp), color = c.muted, modifier = Modifier.padding(top = 8.dp, bottom = 18.dp))

            tools.forEach { t -> ToolCard(t, onDownload = { vm.download(t.id) }, onSkip = { vm.skip(t.id) }) }

        }

        PrimaryButton("Finish setup", onFinish, Modifier.padding(16.dp).fillMaxWidth(), enabled = canFinish, height = 52.d

p, radius = 16.dp)

    }

}

07 Editor, 08 Editor with keyboard (layer 1)



Why: the app's home. Behaviour: the header has the file name, tabs for opened files and undo and
redo only (no Save, no More; it saves automatically). Code area with line numbers, current line
highlight, git change bars in the gutter. When the keyboard is up, a key row sits above it with Tab,
brackets, quotes, arrows. The sidebar can only be opened by swiping right, and the swipe works from
anywhere on the editor. Data: the open file from disk, tabs from vm.openFiles.

@Composable

fun EditorScreen(vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val tabs by vm.openFiles.collectAsState(); val active by vm.activeFile.collectAsState()

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content).statusBarsPadding().imePadding()) {

        Row(Modifier.fillMaxWidth().height(56.dp).padding(start = 18.dp, end = 14.dp), verticalAlignment = Alignment.Center

Vertically) {

            OneLine(active?.name ?: "No file open", CcType.screenTitle, c.text, Modifier.weight(1f))

            HeaderAction("undo", "Undo", enabled = vm.canUndo.collectAsState().value, onClick = vm::undo)

            Spacer(Modifier.width(10.dp))

            HeaderAction("redo", "Redo", enabled = vm.canRedo.collectAsState().value, onClick = vm::redo)

        }

        LazyRow(Modifier.fillMaxWidth().height(40.dp), contentPadding = PaddingValues(horizontal = 12.dp), horizontalArrang

ement = Arrangement.spacedBy(6.dp)) {

            items(tabs, key = { it.path }) { f -> CcChip(f.name, f.path == active?.path) { vm.activate(f) } }

        }

        Box(Modifier.weight(1f)) {

            if (active == null) EmptyState("file", "No file open", "Swipe right and pick a file.")

            else CodeArea(active!!, vm)

        }

        if (WindowInsets.isImeVisible) KeyRow(onKey = vm::insertText)

    }

}

@Composable

fun KeyRow(onKey: (String) -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    LazyRow(Modifier.fillMaxWidth().height(40.dp).background(c.panel), contentPadding = PaddingValues(horizontal = 8.dp, ve

rtical = 4.dp),

        horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(6.dp)) {

        items(listOf("Tab" to "\t", "{" to "{", "}" to "}", "(" to "(", ")" to ")", "[" to "[", "]" to "]", "\"" to "\"", 

";" to ";", "=" to "=", "<" to "<", ">" to ">")) { (label, text) ->

            Box(Modifier.height(32.dp).defaultMinSize(minWidth = 36.dp).clip(RoundedCornerShape(9.dp)).background(c.field)

                .clickable { onKey(text) }.padding(horizontal = 10.dp), contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) {

                Text(label, style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 12.sp, fontWeight = FontWeight.SemiBold), color = c.text2)

            }

        }

    }

}

CodeArea is the app's existing editor view. Keep its logic. Only restyle: mono 11.5 sp, line height 21 sp,
line number column 34 dp wide in faint, current line field, syntax colours from the table, git gutter
bars 3 dp wide.

09 Swipe and 10 Files panel, 11 Files menu

Why: browse and manage project files. Behaviour: title "Files" with the project name under it, buttons
New file and New folder, a filter field, the tree (folders expand with a chevron that turns 90 degrees,
120 ms), git letters on the right. Tap file: opens it and closes the sidebar. Long-press: popup menu.
The Run card sits at the bottom. Data: vm.tree (real folder), vm.gitStatus.

@Composable

fun FilesPanel(vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val project by vm.project.collectAsState(); val rows by vm.visibleTree.collectAsState()

    var filter by remember { mutableStateOf("") }

    SidePanel("Files", project?.name,

        actions = { HeaderAction("plus", "New file") { vm.newFile() }; HeaderAction("folder", "New folder") { vm.newFolder

() } },

        runCard = project?.let { p -> { RunCard(p, vm.branch.collectAsState().value, vm.runState.collectAsState().value) { 

nav.push(Route.Run); vm.run() } } }

    ) {

        CcTextField(filter, { filter = it; vm.setFilter(it) }, Modifier.padding(horizontal = 12.dp, vertical = 10.dp), hint 

= "Filter files", leadingIcon = "search")



        if (rows.isEmpty()) EmptyState("folder", "This folder is empty", "Create a file or a folder.", "New file", vm::newF

ile)

        rows.forEach { n ->

            TreeRow(n, onClick = { if (n.isDir) vm.toggle(n) else { vm.openFile(n); nav.closeSidebar() } },

                    onLongClick = { nav.sheet = Sheet.FileMenu(n.path) })

        }

    }

}

@OptIn(ExperimentalFoundationApi::class)

@Composable

fun TreeRow(n: TreeNode, onClick: () -> Unit, onLongClick: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val rot by animateFloatAsState(if (n.expanded) 90f else 0f, tween(120), label = "chev")

    val (icon, tint) = fileIconFor(n)          // by REAL extension, see the Icons section

    Row(Modifier.fillMaxWidth().padding(horizontal = 8.dp, vertical = 1.dp).height(38.dp).clip(RoundedCornerShape(11.dp))

        .background(if (n.selected) c.selectedFile else Color.Transparent)

        .combinedClickable(onClick = onClick, onLongClick = onLongClick).padding(start = (8 + 16 * n.depth).dp, end = 8.d

p),

        verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {

        if (n.isDir) CcIcon("cr", c.faint, 13.dp, 2.2f, Modifier.rotate(rot)) else Spacer(Modifier.width(13.dp))

        Spacer(Modifier.width(6.dp)); CcIcon(icon, tint, 17.dp, 1.7f); Spacer(Modifier.width(8.dp))

        OneLine(n.name, CcType.small.copy(fontSize = 13.5.sp), c.text2, Modifier.weight(1f))

        n.gitLetter?.let { Text(it, style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 11.sp, fontWeight = FontWeight.Bold), color = when 

(it) { "M" -> c.amber; "A" -> c.green; else -> c.red }) }

    }

}

fun fileIconFor(n: TreeNode): Pair<String, Color> = when {

    n.isDir -> "folder" to LightCcColors.yellow

    n.ext in setOf("kt", "java", "ts", "js", "py", "html", "css", "xml", "json", "gradle", "kts") -> "code" to LightCcColor

s.purple

    else -> "file" to LightCcColors.blue

}

File menu items (show only the ones the app supports): New file, New folder, Rename, Duplicate,
Delete (red, goes through CcConfirmDialog), Copy path. Use CcPopupMenu anchored at the row.

12 Search and 13 Search options (panel, layer 2)

Why: find text in the project. Behaviour: type to search after a 300 ms pause. Chips for match case,
whole word, regex; include and exclude path fields. Results are grouped by file; tap a result: open the
file at that line and close the sidebar. Replace is a toggle that shows a second field and a Replace all
button (asks to confirm). Data: vm.searchResults (real).

@Composable

fun SearchPanel(vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val q by vm.query.collectAsState(); val opts by vm.searchOptions.collectAsState(); val res by vm.searchResults.collectA

sState()

    val project by vm.project.collectAsState()

    SidePanel("Search", project?.name, runCard = project?.let { p -> { RunCard(p, vm.branch.collectAsState().value, vm.runS

tate.collectAsState().value) { nav.push(Route.Run); vm.run() } } }) {

        CcTextField(q, vm::setQuery, Modifier.padding(horizontal = 12.dp, vertical = 10.dp), hint = "Search", leadingIcon = 

"search")

        LazyRow(contentPadding = PaddingValues(horizontal = 12.dp), horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(6.dp)) {

            item { CcChip("Aa", opts.matchCase) { vm.toggleCase() } }

            item { CcChip("Word", opts.wholeWord) { vm.toggleWord() } }

            item { CcChip(".*", opts.regex) { vm.toggleRegex() } }

        }

        when (val r = res) {

            SearchState.Idle -> {}

            SearchState.Running -> LoadingList(3)

            is SearchState.Done -> if (r.groups.isEmpty()) EmptyState("search", "No results", "Try different words or optio

ns.")

                else r.groups.forEach { g ->

                    Text(g.path, style = CcType.section.copy(fontSize = 11.sp), color = c.muted, modifier = Modifier.paddin

g(start = 16.dp, top = 12.dp, bottom = 4.dp), maxLines = 1, overflow = TextOverflow.Ellipsis)

                    g.hits.forEach { h -> ResultCard(h) { vm.openAt(g.path, h.line); nav.closeSidebar() } }

                }

            is SearchState.Failed -> ErrorCard(r.message, onRetry = vm::search)

        }

    }

}



@Composable

fun ResultCard(h: SearchHit, onClick: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val text = buildAnnotatedString {

        append(h.before)

        withStyle(SpanStyle(background = c.matchBg, color = c.matchText)) { append(h.match) }

        append(h.after)

    }

    Row(Modifier.padding(horizontal = 14.dp, vertical = 2.dp).fillMaxWidth().clip(RoundedCornerShape(9.dp)).background(c.co

ntent)

        .clickable(onClick = onClick).padding(horizontal = 9.dp, vertical = 6.dp)) {

        Text("${h.line}", style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 11.sp), color = c.faint, modifier = Modifier.width(26.dp))

        Text(text, style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 11.sp, lineHeight = 15.sp), color = c.text2, maxLines = 1, overflow 

= TextOverflow.Ellipsis)

    }

}

14 GitHub (panel), 15 Not connected, 16 Sign in (full screen)

Why: use GitHub from the phone. Behaviour: if no account is stored the panel shows the empty state
with a Sign in button, which opens the sign-in screen. Sign in shows the real steps of the app's sign-
in flow (for example the device code and the link). When signed in the panel shows the account and
actions (Clone, Source control, History, Pull, Push). Data: vm.github.account.

@Composable

fun GitHubPanel(vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav) {

    val acc by vm.github.account.collectAsState()

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    SidePanel("GitHub", acc?.login) {

        if (acc == null) EmptyState("gh", "Not connected", "Sign in to clone, pull and push.", "Sign in") { nav.push(Route.

GitHubSignIn) }

        else {

            PanelRow("gh", c.text2, acc!!.login, acc!!.name ?: "Signed in") {}

            PanelRow("branch", c.blue, "Clone a repository", null, onClick = { nav.push(Route.Clone) })

            PanelRow("refresh", c.green, "Source control", vm.changeCount.collectAsState().value.let { if (it == 0) "No cha

nges" else "$it changes" }, onClick = { nav.push(Route.SourceControl) })

            PanelRow("history", c.purple, "History", null, onClick = { nav.push(Route.History) })

        }

    }

}

17 Source control, 18 More, 19 History, 20 Commit, 21 Diff (full screens)

Why: the git workflow. Behaviour: Source control shows the branch, Pull and Push small buttons,
then Staged and Changes lists (tap a row to open its diff, tap the tick to stage or unstage), a message
field and Commit (disabled while the message is empty or nothing is staged). The three-dot icon in
this screen is not allowed (no More button): the extra git actions live in the branch row, which opens a
popup menu. History lists the real commits. Commit shows its files. Diff shows green added lines and
red removed lines using the diff tokens. Data: vm.git.* (status, log, show, diff).

@Composable

fun SourceControlScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val st by vm.git.status.collectAsState(); var msg by remember { mutableStateOf("") }

    var menu by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Source control", onBack)

        Row(Modifier.padding(14.dp), verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {

            Box { Row(Modifier.clip(RoundedCornerShape(12.dp)).background(c.field).clickable { menu = true }.padding(horizo

ntal = 12.dp, vertical = 9.dp), verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {

                CcIcon("branch", c.muted, 14.dp); Spacer(Modifier.width(6.dp)); OneLine(st.branch, CcType.small, c.text); S

pacer(Modifier.width(4.dp)); CcIcon("cd", c.faint, 14.dp, 2.2f) }

                CcPopupMenu(menu, { menu = false }, listOf(MenuItem("history", "History") { nav.push(Route.History) }, Menu

Item("refresh", "Refresh") { vm.git.refresh() })) }

            Spacer(Modifier.weight(1f))

            SecondaryButton("Pull", vm.git::pull, icon = "down", height = 40.dp); Spacer(Modifier.width(8.dp))

            SecondaryButton("Push", vm.git::push, icon = "up", height = 40.dp)

        }



        LazyColumn(Modifier.weight(1f)) {

            if (st.isClean) item { EmptyState("check", "No changes", "Your working tree is clean.") }

            if (st.staged.isNotEmpty()) { item { SectionLabel("Staged · ${st.staged.size}") }; items(st.staged, key = { "s" 

+ it.path }) { ChangeRow(it, true, { nav.push(Route.Diff(it.path)) }) { vm.git.unstage(it.path) } } }

            if (st.unstaged.isNotEmpty()) { item { SectionLabel("Changes · ${st.unstaged.size}") }; items(st.unstaged, key 

= { "u" + it.path }) { ChangeRow(it, false, { nav.push(Route.Diff(it.path)) }) { vm.git.stage(it.path) } } }

        }

        Column(Modifier.padding(14.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(10.dp)) {

            CcTextField(msg, { msg = it }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), hint = "Commit message")

            PrimaryButton("Commit", { vm.git.commit(msg); msg = "" }, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), icon = "check", enabled = ms

g.isNotBlank() && st.staged.isNotEmpty())

        }

    }

}

@Composable

fun DiffLine(kind: Char, number: Int?, text: String) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val bg = when (kind) { '+' -> c.diffAddBg; '-' -> c.diffDelBg; else -> Color.Transparent }

    val fg = when (kind) { '+' -> c.diffAddText; '-' -> c.diffDelText; else -> c.text2 }

    Row(Modifier.fillMaxWidth().background(bg).padding(horizontal = 10.dp)) {

        Text(number?.toString() ?: "", style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 10.5.sp), color = c.faint, modifier = Modifier.w

idth(32.dp))

        Text("$kind $text", style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 11.sp), color = fg, softWrap = false)

    }

}

22 Terminal (panel), 23 Terminal session (full screen), 24 New command
(sheet)

Why: run shell commands. Behaviour: the panel lists the real sessions with a green dot for running;
tapping one opens the full screen session. The session is a real shell: output area (mono 12, scrolls to
the end), input row, key row with Tab, Ctrl, Esc and arrows. The New command sheet has a field and
the user's recent and saved commands; Run sends it to the shell. Data: vm.terminal.sessions, vm.termina
l.output(id), vm.savedCommands.

@Composable

fun TerminalSessionScreen(origin: String?, id: String, name: String, vm: MainViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val lines by vm.terminal.output(id).collectAsState(emptyList()); var input by remember { mutableStateOf("") }

    val listState = rememberLazyListState()

    LaunchedEffect(lines.size) { if (lines.isNotEmpty()) listState.animateScrollToItem(lines.lastIndex) }

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content).imePadding()) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, name, onBack, actions = { HeaderAction("trash", "Clear") { vm.terminal.clear(id) } })

        LazyColumn(Modifier.weight(1f).background(c.field).padding(10.dp), state = listState) {

            items(lines) { Text(it.text, style = CcType.log.copy(fontSize = 12.sp), color = if (it.isError) c.red else c.te

xt2) }

        }

        LazyRow(Modifier.height(40.dp).padding(horizontal = 8.dp, vertical = 4.dp), horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spa

cedBy(6.dp)) {

            items(listOf("Tab" to "\t", "Esc" to "\u001B", "Ctrl" to "", "↑" to "\u001B[A", "↓" to "\u001B[B", "←" to "\u00

1B[D", "→" to "\u001B[C")) { (l, s) ->

                Box(Modifier.height(32.dp).clip(RoundedCornerShape(9.dp)).background(c.field).clickable { vm.terminal.send

(id, s) }.padding(horizontal = 12.dp), contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) { Text(l, style = CcType.code.copy(fontSize = 1

2.sp, fontWeight = FontWeight.SemiBold), color = c.text2) } }

        }

        Row(Modifier.padding(10.dp), verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {

            CcTextField(input, { input = it }, Modifier.weight(1f), hint = "Type a command", mono = true)

            Spacer(Modifier.width(8.dp))

            Box(Modifier.size(44.dp).clip(RoundedCornerShape(13.dp)).background(c.accent).clickable { vm.terminal.send(id, 

input + "\n"); input = "" }, contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) { CcIcon("send", Color.White, 18.dp, 2f) }

        }

    }

}

25 Run and build, 26 Build finished (full screens)

Why: build and install the app. Behaviour: Run opens the screen at once and starts the real build.
Steps appear as the build reports them; each step shows a spinner, then a green tick or a red cross. A
progress bar shows the real percent. Cancel stops the build. When it ends: Ready shows a green



badge, time taken, Open app (green) and Share; Failed shows a red badge with the real error text and
a Problems button. Data: vm.build.state.

@Composable

fun RunScreen(origin: String?, vm: MainViewModel, nav: AppNav, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val s by vm.build.state.collectAsState()

    LaunchedEffect(s) { if (s is BuildState.Done) { nav.stack.removeLastOrNull(); nav.push(Route.BuildFinished) } }

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Run", onBack)

        (s as? BuildState.Running)?.let { r ->

            Column(Modifier.padding(16.dp)) {

                ProgressLine(r.currentStep, r.percent / 100f, "${r.percent}%")

                Spacer(Modifier.height(12.dp))

                r.steps.forEach { st -> Row(Modifier.padding(vertical = 4.dp), verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertical

ly) {

                    when (st.state) { StepState.Done -> CcIcon("check", c.green, 16.dp, 2.4f); StepState.Failed -> CcIcon

("x", c.red, 16.dp, 2.4f); else -> CircularProgressIndicator(Modifier.size(14.dp), color = c.accent, strokeWidth = 2.dp) }

                    Spacer(Modifier.width(10.dp)); Text(st.name, style = CcType.small, color = c.text2) } }

                Spacer(Modifier.height(12.dp)); SecondaryButton("Cancel", vm.build::cancel, Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), destru

ctive = true)

            }

        }

    }

}

27 Website preview, 28 Console, 29 Compose previews (full screens)

Why: see the result without leaving the app. Preview: a WebView of the local page with an address pill
and a reload icon. Console: the page's console.* lines coloured by level (error red, warn amber, others
text2). Compose previews: a list of the @Preview functions the project really has; empty state when
none.

30 Logcat, 31 Problems (panels)

Why: see the app's logs and the code's errors. Behaviour: Logcat streams the real device log; chips
filter by level; each line is time, level letter (coloured), tag, message, in mono 10.5 sp. Problems lists
real errors and warnings grouped by file; tap a row: opens the file at the line and closes the sidebar.
Data: vm.logcat, vm.problems.

32 Settings and 33 to 44 Settings pages (full screens)

Why: control the app. Behaviour: opening Settings (rail, bottom) pushes the categories screen.
Tapping a category pushes its page and the header reads "Settings General" with the back button.
Every toggle and value writes to the real settings store at once (DataStore). Show only rows that match
features the app has. The pages are General, Editor, Code intelligence, Build and toolchain, Terminal,
GitHub, Appearance, Storage, Security, About, Developer. Rows that run an action (Clear cache,
Delete build tools, Crash test) ask to confirm first with CcConfirmDialog.

@Composable

fun SettingsScreen(origin: String?, nav: AppNav, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Settings", onBack)

        Column(Modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()).padding(bottom = 24.dp)) {

            SettingsGroup("App") {

                SettingRow("cog", c.blue, "General", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("General")) })

                SettingRow("code", c.purple, "Editor", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Editor")) })

                SettingRow("flask", c.yellow, "Code intelligence", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Code intelligen

ce")) })

                SettingRow("play", c.green, "Build and toolchain", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Build and toolc

hain")) })

                SettingRow("term", c.blue, "Terminal", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Terminal")) })



                SettingRow("gh", c.text2, "Git and GitHub", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Git and GitHub")) })

                SettingRow("moon", c.purple, "Appearance", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Appearance")) })

                SettingRow("db", c.orange, "Storage", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Storage")) })

                SettingRow("lock", c.teal, "Security", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("Security")) })

                SettingRow("info", c.faint, "About", onClick = { nav.push(Route.SettingsPage("About")) }, showDivider = fal

se)

            }

        }

    }

}

/** Example of one page: every value is read from and written to the real settings store. */

@Composable

fun EditorSettingsPage(origin: String?, vm: SettingsViewModel, onBack: () -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    val s by vm.editor.collectAsState()

    Column(Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(c.content)) {

        ScreenHeader(origin, "Editor", onBack)

        Column(Modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState())) {

            SettingsGroup("Text") {

                SettingRow("code", c.purple, "Font size", value = "${s.fontSize}", onClick = vm::pickFontSize)

                SettingRow("menu", c.blue, "Word wrap", "Wrap long lines", trailing = { CcToggle(s.wordWrap, vm::setWordWra

p) })

                SettingRow("check", c.green, "Show line numbers", trailing = { CcToggle(s.lineNumbers, vm::setLineNumbers) 

}, showDivider = false)

            }

        }

    }

}

All the other pages are built exactly the same way: ScreenHeader, then one or more SettingsGroups with Set
tingRows, values read from the store.

45 Project settings (full screen)

Why: edit the project's name, colour, package id, SDK versions and build variants. Behaviour: the
header shows the project name in bold and "Project settings" muted. A colour picker row lets the user
choose a project colour from the six tile colours; the letter updates from the name. Edits save at once.
Data: the real project and its Gradle files.

Screens that are not in this document

The app has more screens than are written here. Build each one with the same components from 2.3:
ScreenHeader (with back and origin), SettingsGroup and SettingRow for option screens, PanelRow for lists, CcTex
tField for input, PrimaryButton and SecondaryButton for actions, CcBottomSheet, CcPopupMenu and CcConfirmDialog
for choices, and EmptyState, LoadingList, ErrorCard for the three states. Keep the existing logic. Only
change the look and the way the screen opens and closes. If a screen needs an icon that is not in CcIc
onPaths, add its path text to the map using the same 24 by 24 rules.

2.7 Project settings: App icon, Signing keys and Self-test
(screens 45 to 51)

These screens exist in the app today as rows (App icon, Debug key, Release key, Self-test). This
section says what happens when each row is opened. Every value in the pictures is an example.
Everything shown must be read from the real project and the real device.

45 Project settings (the screen that opens them)



The App group has App name, Package name and App icon (a small preview of the real icon on the
right, then a chevron). The Signing group has Debug key (green "Ready") and Release key (amber
"Not set", or green "Ready" when a key exists). Tapping App icon opens screen 46. Tapping either
key row opens screen 47 (or 48 when a release key already exists).

46 App icon

What it is: the place where the user gives the app its launcher icon. The user does not choose from
ready-made icon types. The user picks their own picture and the app makes every size the project
needs.

How it opens: a full screen, header "Project settings" (bold) and "App icon" (muted). At the top a card
shows the current icon of this project (read from the project's res/mipmap folder; if the project has
none, show the default Android icon and the text "No icon yet") and three small previews of the same
icon as a circle, a rounded square and a square, because phones crop icons differently.

What the user can do: 1. Tap Choose an image. The Android file picker opens (ActivityResultContracts.
PickVisualMedia for the gallery or OpenDocument for Files). The user picks a square PNG or JPG. 1024 by
1024 is best; 512 by 512 is the smallest. If it is smaller or not square the screen shows a red line with
the real reason and does not apply it. (A non-square picture can be cropped to the centre square.) 2.
Choose a background colour from the six project colours. It fills behind a picture that has transparent
edges. 3. The three preview icons update at once. 4. Tap Apply to project. The app writes the icon
files into the project (see code). The row in Project settings shows the new icon. Tap Reset to go back
to what the project had.

Where the files go: res/mipmap-mdpi (48 px), hdpi (72), xhdpi (96), xxhdpi (144), xxxhdpi (192): ic_launcher.png
and ic_launcher_round.png in each. For adaptive icons also res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml with the
foreground picture and res/values/ic_launcher_background.xml with the colour.

suspend fun applyIcon(project: Project, source: Uri, background: Int, ctx: Context) = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {

    val bmp = ctx.contentResolver.openInputStream(source).use { BitmapFactory.decodeStream(it) }

        ?: error("This file is not a readable picture")

    require(minOf(bmp.width, bmp.height) >= 512) { "The picture is too small. Use at least 512 by 512." }

    val side = minOf(bmp.width, bmp.height)

    val square = Bitmap.createBitmap(bmp, (bmp.width - side) / 2, (bmp.height - side) / 2, side, side)

    val sizes = mapOf("mdpi" to 48, "hdpi" to 72, "xhdpi" to 96, "xxhdpi" to 144, "xxxhdpi" to 192)

    sizes.forEach { (density, px) ->

        val dir = File(project.dir, "app/src/main/res/mipmap-$density").apply { mkdirs() }

        val scaled = Bitmap.createScaledBitmap(square, px, px, true)

        File(dir, "ic_launcher.png").outputStream().use { scaled.compress(Bitmap.CompressFormat.PNG, 100, it) }

        File(dir, "ic_launcher_round.png").outputStream().use { roundOf(scaled).compress(Bitmap.CompressFormat.PNG, 100, i

t) }

    }

    File(project.dir, "app/src/main/res/values/ic_launcher_background.xml").writeText(

        """<resources><color name="ic_launcher_background">#%06X</color></resources>""".format(background and 0xFFFFFF))

}

Empty and error states: no icon yet (default icon and text), picture too small or unreadable (red line,
nothing is written), write failed (real error with Retry).

47 Signing keys (Debug key and Release key)

First the idea, in plain words, because it is easy to mix up:



Debug key Release key

What it is A key the app makes by itself The real key of the app, made by the user (or imported)
the first time it builds

Used for Installing test builds on the Publishing to Google Play and every later update
user's own phone

Can No Yes
publish to
Play

Who Nobody, it is automatic The user, once. The app can generate it for the user (button "Create
creates it a new key") or the user can import one made before

If lost Nothing happens, a new one The app can never be updated on Google Play under the same
is made listing. Back it up

How it opens: two cards. The Debug key card says "Made by the app, automatically", shows a green
Ready pill and its fingerprint, and has no buttons. The Release key card says "Needed to publish" and
has an amber "Not set" pill with two buttons: Create a new key and Import a key file. Under the cards
a small text says keys stay on this phone in the app's private storage and are never uploaded.

Can the key be imported? Yes. Android signing keys are normal files: .jks, .keystore or .p12 (PKCS12).
Many developers already have one. Can the app make it automatically? Yes. Create a new key
makes the key on the phone with a strong random password and keeps it in the app's private storage.
The user can still change the password. Either way, the app tells the user to back it up.

Where it is kept: the key file is copied into the app's private folder (filesDir/keys/<project id>/release.jk
s). Passwords are not saved as plain text. They are encrypted with a key held by the Android Keystore
system (EncryptedSharedPreferences or Tink) and only when "Remember the password on this phone" is
on. Never write the password to a log.

48 Release key (ready)

Opens when a release key exists. Shows the real alias, the date it is valid until, the owner (CN), the
SHA-256 fingerprint and the key file name. Buttons: Back up (opens the Android share sheet or save
dialog with the .jks file so the user can store it safely), Replace (asks to confirm, then goes to Create
or Import), Remove from this phone (red, confirm dialog that repeats the warning that the key cannot
be recovered unless it was backed up). An amber warning card keeps telling the user to back it up.

49 Create a key

Fields: Key alias (default release), Your name, Country code (two letters), Valid for (25, 30 or 50 years,
25 is selected), Password (made by the app, can be changed), toggle "Remember the password on
this phone" (on by default). Create key is disabled until the alias, name and country code are valid
and the password has at least 6 characters. While it works it shows a progress line. On success it
opens screen 48. On failure it shows the real error.

suspend fun createReleaseKey(p: Project, alias: String, name: String, country: String, years: Int, password: CharArray): Ke

yInfo =

    withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {

        val file = File(ctx.filesDir, "keys/${p.id}/release.jks").apply { parentFile!!.mkdirs() }

        // uses the keytool of the build tools the app already has

        val cmd = listOf(keytool, "-genkeypair", "-v", "-keystore", file.path, "-alias", alias,

            "-keyalg", "RSA", "-keysize", "2048", "-validity", (years * 365).toString(),

            "-storepass", String(password), "-keypass", String(password),

            "-dname", "CN=$name, C=$country")



        val r = runProcess(cmd)

        if (r.exitCode != 0) { file.delete(); error(r.stderr.lastLine()) }

        secrets.save(p.id, alias, password)          // only if the toggle is on

        readKeyInfo(file, password, alias)

    }

50 Import a key

Step 1: Choose key file opens the file picker (OpenDocument with .jks, .keystore, .p12). The picked name
and size show in a card. Step 2: Store password. When the user types it and leaves the field, the app
tries to open the file and lists the keys inside (alias and fingerprint) as radio rows. A wrong password
shows "Wrong password" in red under the field. Step 3: Key password (optional, empty means the
same as the store password). Import key copies the file into the private folder and opens screen 48.

fun openKeystore(file: File, storePass: CharArray): KeyStore {

    for (type in listOf("PKCS12", "JKS")) {

        try { return KeyStore.getInstance(type).apply { file.inputStream().use { load(it, storePass) } } } catch (_: Except

ion) {}

    }

    error("Wrong password or not a key file")

}

fun aliasesOf(ks: KeyStore) = ks.aliases().toList().filter { ks.isKeyEntry(it) }

51 Self-test

What it is: a quick health check of the app on this phone, found in Settings, Developer, Self-test. It
exists so the user (or the developer) can see why a build or a feature fails without reading logs.

How it opens: a full screen, header "Developer" (bold) and "Self-test" (muted). It runs the checks at
once. A summary card at the top says "15 passed · 1 to check" and the time it took, with a Run again
button. Under it is the list, one row per check, each with a green tick, an amber triangle (needs
attention but not fatal, for example "Shell tools: not installed, optional") or a red cross (fails), a short
title and one sentence that says the result in plain words. At the bottom Share report shares the
results as text (version, self-test and the last 200 log lines).

The 16 checks are the real ones the app already has. The rows in the picture are examples. Do not
add or invent checks. Each check returns Pass, Warn(message) or Fail(message); the list shows them in the
order they ran.

sealed interface CheckResult { data object Pass : CheckResult; data class Warn(val msg: String) : CheckResult; data class F

ail(val msg: String) : CheckResult }

data class Check(val title: String, val passText: String, val run: suspend () -> CheckResult)

2.8 Icons: logo, project icons and icon packs (NEW FEATURE,
screens 52 to 57)

This is a new feature. It is not in the app today. Build it only after the restyle is finished, and do not let
it change anything that already works. Like everything else: build exactly what the pictures show and
invent nothing. The design is our own. It must not be copied from any other app, so keep the names,
wording and layout exactly as written here.



What it is for: one place to manage the icons of the open project: the app logo (screen 46), the
project's own icons, and icon packs the user can get and use without internet.

How it opens: Project settings has a new row Icons (App group, under App icon, sub line "Logo,
project icons and icon packs"). It opens a full screen with the header "Project settings" (bold) and
"Icons" (muted). At the top is a segmented control (the same component as in Components) with
three parts: This project, Browse, Code. Back goes to Project settings.

52 and 53 This project

Logo card at the top (radius 22, panel colour, 1 dp border, padding 16): the project's real launcher
icon at 84 by 84 (radius 24) on the left; on the right the title "Your logo", the line "Shown on the
phone home screen and in the Play Store." and a small accent button Change logo. The button
opens screen 46 (the app logo screen). If the project has no logo, the left tile is a dashed grey
outline with an image icon, the title is "No logo yet", the line is "Your app uses the default Android
icon." and the button reads Choose your logo.
Icons in this project · N: one grouped list (settings-group style). Each row: tile 36 with the icon, the
file name, and the line "Vector · 24 dp" (the real kind and size). N is the real count. Tap a row for a
sheet to rename, copy as code or delete (delete asks to confirm). The last row, Add an SVG file
("Turns it into an Android vector"), opens the file picker for .svg files. The app converts the file to
an Android vector drawable in res/drawable. If it cannot be converted, show the real reason in a red
line.
Empty (53): the text "No icons in this project. Add an SVG file, or open Browse to take icons from
a pack." with an Add an SVG file button.

54 Browse, getting a pack

A short line says a pack is downloaded once and then works without internet. Icon packs is one
grouped list. Two packs are offered at launch, and only these two:

1. Material Symbols (Google's Android icon set, about 4,304 icons, Outlined style, weight 400,
Apache 2.0). It is the main pack and matches the look of Android and Compose.

2. Lucide (the most popular community line-icon set, about 1,500 icons, ISC licence). It gives a
clean, modern alternative.

Each row shows the name, the number of icons and the download size, and a Get button (outlined pill,
accent). While a pack downloads, its row shows a progress bar with the real percent and size, and the
button becomes a red Stop. A downloaded pack shows a tick instead of Get. A failed download
shows the real message and a Retry. The picture shows Material Symbols at 62% and Lucide waiting.
The icon counts and sizes in the picture are examples: show the real numbers from the index file.

The list comes from one small index file the app downloads (packs.json: id, name, icon count, size, url,
licence). Do not type the list into the app. This way a third pack can be added later without an app
update. Keep both licence texts in About.

Building the two pack files (one time, by the developer, not in the app): - Material Symbols: use the
Outlined, weight 400, 24 px SVGs. Their canvas is 960 units (viewBox="0 -960 960 960"), so scale every
path to the 24 by 24 grid when you build the pack file, or write the vector with viewportWidth=960, viewpor
tHeight=960 and shift it down by 960. If you skip this the icons will be huge or off-screen. - Lucide: its
SVGs are 24 by 24 line icons (stroke 2, round caps and joins, no fill). The pack file must keep a style



field ("fill" or "stroke"). When saving to the project, write android:fillColor for fill packs, and android:stro
keColor, android:strokeWidth="2", android:strokeLineCap="round" and android:strokeLineJoin="round" with no fill
for stroke packs. In the Compose code use addPath(... stroke = SolidColor(...), strokeLineWidth = 2f, stro
keLineCap = StrokeCap.Round, strokeLineJoin = StrokeJoin.Round). Draw Lucide icons in the grid with stroke
too, not filled.

55 Browse, a pack is ready

A Pack selector row (tap to choose between the downloaded packs, Material Symbols or Lucide; only
downloaded packs are listed, and if none is downloaded show "Get a pack in Browse" with a button to
the pack list), a field "Find an icon", a line such as "4,304 icons · tap one to use it" (the real count of
the chosen pack), and one rounded surface with the icons in 5 columns (icons only, no boxes, each
cell 52 tall, radius 14). The tapped icon gets a soft accent background and a 2 dp accent outline.
Searching filters by name after 150 ms. Use a LazyVerticalGrid so 4,304 icons stay smooth. Give every
cell the icon name as its accessibility description.

56 Use this icon (bottom sheet)

Title "Use this icon". A large preview band with the icon and its name and pack. Six colour dots. A
segmented control for size (24, 32 or 48 dp). A File name field (default ic_<name>; lower case letters,
numbers and underscores only; red line if the name already exists). Two buttons: Copy code and
Save to project (writes res/drawable/<name>.xml, closes the sheet, toast "Saved").

57 Code

Shows the Compose code (ImageVector) of the selected saved icon in a mono block, then Saved icons ·
N as a list with ticks. The button at the bottom reads Copy code for N icons. Empty state: "Icons you
save appear here as code."

// ---- data

data class IconPack(val id: String, val name: String, val count: Int, val bytes: Long, val url: String,

                    val style: String)                      // "fill" (Material Symbols) or "stroke" (Lucide)

data class LibIcon(val name: String, val pathData: String, val style: String)   // 24 x 24 grid

// ---- download once, then keep on the phone

suspend fun downloadPack(pack: IconPack, onProgress: (Float) -> Unit): File = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {

    val out = File(ctx.filesDir, "iconpacks/${pack.id}.json").apply { parentFile!!.mkdirs() }

    val tmp = File(out.path + ".part")

    http.newCall(Request.Builder().url(pack.url).build()).execute().use { r ->

        check(r.isSuccessful) { "Download failed (${r.code})" }

        val total = r.body!!.contentLength().takeIf { it > 0 } ?: pack.bytes

        r.body!!.byteStream().use { input -> tmp.outputStream().use { o ->

            val buf = ByteArray(16 * 1024); var done = 0L

            while (true) { val n = input.read(buf); if (n < 0) break; o.write(buf, 0, n); done += n

                onProgress((done.toFloat() / total).coerceIn(0f, 1f)); ensureActive() } } }

    }

    tmp.renameTo(out); out

}

// ---- SVG path data -> Android vector drawable file

fun toVectorXml(icon: LibIcon, colorHex: String, sizeDp: Int) = """<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/re

s/android"

    android:width="${sizeDp}dp" android:height="${sizeDp}dp" android:viewportWidth="24" android:viewportHeight="24">

    ${if (icon.style == "fill")

        """<path android:fillColor="$colorHex" android:pathData="${icon.pathData}"/>"""

      else

        """<path android:strokeColor="$colorHex" android:strokeWidth="2" android:strokeLineCap="round"

        android:strokeLineJoin="round" android:pathData="${icon.pathData}"/>"""}

</vector>"""

suspend fun addToProject(p: Project, icon: LibIcon, fileName: String, colorHex: String, sizeDp: Int) = withContext(Dispatch

ers.IO) {



    require(Regex("[a-z][a-z0-9_]*").matches(fileName)) { "Use lower case letters, numbers and underscores" }

    val f = File(p.dir, "app/src/main/res/drawable/$fileName.xml")

    require(!f.exists()) { "A file with this name already exists" }

    f.parentFile!!.mkdirs(); f.writeText(toVectorXml(icon, colorHex, sizeDp))

}

// ---- Compose code for the same icon

fun toComposeCode(icon: LibIcon, name: String, sizeDp: Int) = """val AppIcons.$name: ImageVector by lazy {

    ImageVector.Builder("$name", ${sizeDp}.dp, ${sizeDp}.dp, 24f, 24f).addPath(

        pathData = PathParser().parsePathString("${icon.pathData}").toNodes(),

        ${if (icon.style == "fill") "fill = SolidColor(Color.Black)"

          else "stroke = SolidColor(Color.Black), strokeLineWidth = 2f, strokeLineCap = StrokeCap.Round, strokeLineJoin = S

trokeJoin.Round"}

    ).build()

}"""

// ---- the grid

@Composable

fun IconGrid(icons: List<LibIcon>, onTap: (LibIcon) -> Unit) {

    val c = CcTheme.colors

    LazyVerticalGrid(GridCells.Fixed(3), contentPadding = PaddingValues(16.dp),

        horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp), verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp)) {

        items(icons, key = { it.name }) { i ->

            Column(Modifier.clip(RoundedCornerShape(18.dp)).background(c.field).clickable { onTap(i) }.padding(vertical = 1

4.dp),

                horizontalAlignment = Alignment.CenterHorizontally) {

                Icon(rememberVector(i.pathData), null, tint = c.text2, modifier = Modifier.size(26.dp))

                Spacer(Modifier.height(9.dp))

                OneLine(i.name.replace('_', ' '), CcType.caption, c.textSoft, Modifier.padding(horizontal = 6.dp))

            }

        }

    }

}

Tab bar code: use TabRow with containerColor = c.content, contentColor = c.accent, a 2 dp indicator in
accent, and divider 1 dp in c.divider. Unselected tab text is c.muted.

Rules for this feature: nothing is typed in (icon names, counts, sizes and project icons all come from
the real pack index, the real downloaded file and the real project folder); works offline after the first
download; never block the screen while a download runs (the user can leave and come back, the
download continues in a foreground service or WorkManager); show the real error text if anything
fails.

2.6 Build order for the developer

1. Add fonts. Add CcTheme.kt. Add CcIcons.kt. Check an icon renders.
2. Add the components in 2.3 and look at them on one test screen.
3. Add AppNav, SidebarHost, ToolRail, SidePanel and wire them in MainScreen. Check swipe, close, Back,
double Back to exit.

4. Restyle the existing screens one by one, replacing old UI with the components. Do not touch
their logic.

5. Add the empty, loading and error states to every list.
6. Test with zero projects, one project and many projects. Test the keyboard. Test large font size.

PART 3. THE VISUAL SPEC

Read this first



CloseCode is a working app with many features already built. This document changes how it looks
and how screens connect. It must not remove, break or replace any feature that already works.

Scope

Follow the mockups exactly. Build exactly what the mockup pictures and the numbers in this
document show: the same spacing, sizes, icons, colours, corners, order of items and texts. Do not
invent anything that is not described here. Do not add, remove, move, resize, recolour or rename
anything because it seems better. Do not use a library default look (Material default colours, shapes,
icon sets, fonts, elevations) where this document gives a value. If something is missing or two things
seem to disagree, keep the existing behaviour of the app, copy the closest mockup, and ask. Before
you call a screen finished, put your screenshot next to the mockup picture and compare spacing,
icons and text one by one. Everything in the pictures that is a name, number or list is an example and
must come from real data.

OpenCode must not be included in this development. Leave everything about it exactly as it is
today.
Do not add features that are not already in the app. Only restyle what exists and add the navigation
rules below.

Real data only (no fake content)

The pictures use example names so the layout can be seen. Every name, number, date, list and state
in a picture is an example. Nothing in the app may be hard-coded to match a picture. Read every
value from where the app already gets it:

Shown in a picture Must come from

Project names, letters, colours, The user's real projects on this phone (created, cloned or imported by the user).
types, last-opened times The letter is the first letter of the real name. Tile colour is stored per project or

derived from the name. Empty list when there are none

Recent projects and project Real project list sorted by last opened
counts

File tree, open files, tabs, file The real project folder and real open-file state. Icon by real extension
icons

Code, line numbers, cursor The real file content in the editor

Git marks (M, A, D), counts, The real repository (git status, log, diff)
branch, commits, authors,
hashes, times, diffs

GitHub account, repositories The real signed-in account. Not signed in means the not-connected screen

Problems, errors, warnings Real results of the project's checks and build

Build steps, percentages, The real running build
sizes, times, file names

Logcat and Console lines The real log stream

Terminal output, sessions, Real shells and the user's saved commands
saved commands

Versions, build number, Real values from the app and device
storage sizes, download
progress



Shown in a picture Must come from

Settings values and toggles The real saved settings (toggle shows what is saved and saves on change)

Package name, SDK levels, The real project configuration
version name and code

Templates The real list of templates the app ships with

If a value does not exist yet, show the empty state (see States), never an example. No placeholder
projects, no demo files, no sample repositories, no fake commits.

Not every screen is shown here

The app already has more screens and features than the pictures cover. The pictures are a design
system, not a full screen list. Any screen or feature that is not shown must be restyled with the same
design: same colours, type, spacing, shapes, icons, components and navigation rules from this
document. See "Screens that are not shown" for the recipe. Do not leave an old-style screen next to
new-style screens, and do not remove a screen because it has no picture.

How to read the numbers

All sizes are in dp (px in the pictures equal dp) on a 360 dp wide phone. Text is in sp. Where a picture
and a number here differ, the number wins. Scale spacing together on wider phones.

Design numbers

Define every value once as a theme token and use the token everywhere. No screen may contain a
loose hex colour, font size or corner radius.

Colours (light theme)

Token Hex Used for

rail #E3E5EA Left tool rail, status bar area, outer background behind the panel

panel #F1F2F5 Side panel, bottom sheets, popup menus

content #FAFAFB Editor and every full screen background. Never pure white

field #E9EBEF Text fields, grouped settings cards, unselected chips, key row
keys, back button, result cards

selectedRow #DCDFE5 Selected row in lists

selectedFile #DDE0FB Selected file in the tree (text #2E3036)

border #D5D8DE Card, menu and sheet borders (1 dp)

divider #E3E5EA Lines between header and content, between rows (1 dp)

toggleOff #B8BCC5 Toggle track when off

text #1F2024 Titles, main text

text2 #2E3036 Body text, code text



Token Hex Used for

textSoft #4F535C Secondary button text, unselected chip text

muted #626772 Descriptions, sub lines, section labels

faint #858A95 Line numbers, hints, disabled icons

accent #5865F2 Primary buttons, selected rail item, selected chip, links, toggle on,
progress, focus ring

green #248046 Run button, success, added lines, "Ready"

amber #C98A0A Modified, warnings

red #DA373C Errors, delete, badges, "Not installed"

blue #2F6FE0 Info and config file icons

purple #7B5CE0 Code file icons

yellow #D99A06 Folder icons

teal #1F9D6B Success icons

orange #D97706 Warning triangle

pink #DB4C9B Image icon

diffAddBg / #DDF3E4 / #1A7F37 Added lines
diffAddText

diffDelBg / #FBE4E5 / #DA373C Removed lines, error rows
diffDelText

matchBg / #FBE7A1 / #6B4E00 Search match highlight
matchText

dim rgba(30,35,50,0.30) Layer behind sheets and menus (0.38 behind first-time dialogs,
0.18 behind small menus)

shadow rgba(30,35,50,0.25), Popup menus and the sliding editor card
blur 30, y 12

Icon tile tint: the tile behind a coloured icon is the icon colour at 13% opacity (hex alpha 22).

Syntax colours (light): keyword #8250DF, type #1B7C83, string #A5461D, function #6F5A00, number
#0A7D4F, comment #5E7F46, variable #0A5EA8, plain #2E3036. Apply only to real code tokens of
the file's language. Plain text and Markdown stay plain.

Project tile colours: each project has its own colour (saved with the project or derived from its name
from this set: #2563EB, #16A34A, #EA580C, #0E7490, #7C3AED, #BE185D). Letter on the tile is
white, weight 800.

Type

UI font Inter. Code and terminal font JetBrains Mono. Line height 1.4 of the size unless noted.

Style Size / weight Used for

Hero 33 sp / 800, tracking -1 Welcome headline

Setup title 27 sp / 800 First-time setup title

Panel title 21 to 22 sp / 800 Title at the top of a side panel



Style Size / weight Used for

Sheet title 19 to 20 sp / 800 Bottom sheet titles

Screen title 16.5 sp / 700 Header title of full screens

Item title 14.5 sp / 600 List and settings row titles

Body 14 sp / 400 to 500 Buttons in menus, descriptions

Small 13 to 13.5 sp Field text, tree rows

Caption 12 to 12.5 sp Sub lines, labels above fields

Section label 11 sp / 700, uppercase, tracking 0.8 Group titles

Code 11.5 sp mono, line height 21 Editor

Terminal and logs 10.5 to 12 sp mono Terminal, Logcat, Console

Spacing and shape

Screen side padding 14 to 18. Row padding 8 by 14. Gap between related items 8 to 12.
Radius: tiles 13 to 15, buttons 12 to 16, cards 18 to 20, grouped settings cards 18, chips and pill
fields 15 to 22, sheets 26 (top corners), panel 26 (top-left), phone preview 30.
Borders 1 dp. Selected outline 2 dp accent. Focus ring 1.5 dp accent.
Status bar area 34 dp. Header 56 dp. Home indicator area 16 dp.

Motion

Sidebar swipe: the editor card follows the finger, rests 300 dp to the right, spring (damping 0.85,
stiffness 400). Release past 40% opens; otherwise it snaps back.
Sheets slide up in 250 ms ease-out. Menus fade and scale from 0.95 in 120 ms.
Screen push slides in from the right in 220 ms; back reverses it.
Toggle knob 160 ms. Progress bars animate 200 ms between values.
Respect the system setting for reduced animation.

Icons

All icons are simple line icons on a 24 by 24 grid, drawn as vectors (SVG path or Compose
ImageVector) with stroke width 1.8 (2.2 for chevrons and back, 2.4 for ticks), round caps, round joins,
no fill (only Play is filled). Colour is the token named in the table. Use these everywhere in the app. If
the app uses an icon that is not in this list, draw a new one in the same style (same grid, same stroke,
rounded) and add it to your icon set.

Icon sizes

Place Size Stroke

Rail tool icon 22 1.8

Back button chevron 20 2.2

Header action (undo, redo, share, clear) 17 to 19 1.9



Place Size Stroke

Panel action button (plus, folder, refresh) 17 to 18 1.9

List and settings tile 18 (settings) / 21 (panel rows) 1.8

Button icon 15 to 17 2.0

Run button play 17 filled none

Tree row icon 17 to 18 1.7

Chevron in rows 15 to 17 2.2

Tick in lists 18 2.4

Empty-state and hero icon 36 to 38 1.6

Badge glyph 10 to 12 3

Touch target for any icon button is at least 38 by 38 dp (44 preferred).

